        <senderName>Environment Canada</senderName>
        <headline>red warning - tornado - in effect</headline>
        <description>At 8:47 p.m. Central Standard Time Sunday, Environment Canada has updated a tornado warning for Southwestern Saskatchewan. Extra care and attention should be exercised. The following localities are included in the warning: Leader, Gull Lake, Piapot and Fox Valley. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are also possible.</description>
        <instruction>Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</instruction>
        <web>https://weather.gc.ca/</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:EC-MSC-SMC:1.0:Alert_Type</valueName>
