            <valueName>layer:SOREM:1.0:Broadcast_Text</valueName>
            <value>At 8:47 p.m. Central Standard Time Sunday, Environment Canada has updated a tornado warning for Southwestern Saskatchewan. Extra care and attention should be exercised. The following localities are included in the warning: Leader, Gull Lake, Piapot and Fox Valley. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are also possible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</value>
        </parameter>
